<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n3074" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Ăpŏnus</span></b> , i,
			m., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄπονος</span>
		(pain-curing). <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>A warm</i>, <i>medicinal fountain in
				the vicinity of Padua</i>, now <i>Bagni d'
			Albano</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Patavinorum aquae calidae,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					2, 103, 106, § 227</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Aponi fons,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Suet. Tib. 14</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Aponi fontes,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Mart.
					6, 42, 4</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Cassiod. Var. 2, 39</span></i>; cf. Mann.
			Ital. 1, 91.—Hence, </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Ăpŏ-nus</span></b> ,
				a, um, adj., <i>Aponian</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">tellus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Mart.
					1, 62, 3</span></i>
			: Aponinus, dub. in Vop. Firm. Sat. c. 3.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
